# NoID Privacy Workstation — .gitignore
#
# Rationale: keep repo lean + prevent accidental commits of secrets,
# build artifacts, host-specific data, and large binaries.
# GitHub.com warns above 50 MiB and blocks regular Git-repository files above
# 100 MiB. Release assets are a separate surface and must each be under 2 GiB.

# ============================================================
# Build artifacts + large binaries
# ============================================================

# Fedora live-ISO base images (10+ GB each) — download via build script,
# do NOT commit. Use `curl` + SHA256 verify in docs/build.md instead.
image/*.iso
image/*.img
image/*.qcow2
image/*.raw
image/*.vmdk

# Build output (livemedia-creator working directory + final ISO)
*.log
build/
output/
build-output/
build-archive/
*.iso
*.img
*.iso.sha256
*.iso.asc
*.iso.sig
SHA256SUMS
SHA256SUMS.asc
BUILD-ATTESTATION.txt
vm-test-signoff.txt

# Kickstart temp files
*.ks.bak
*.ks.orig
*.ks.bak-*

# Per-file backups (snapshots before refactors)
*.bak-*
.bak-*

# ============================================================
# Secrets + credentials (MUST never leak)
# ============================================================

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# SSH keys
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
id_dsa
*.pem
*.key
authorized_keys
known_hosts

# GPG keys
*.gpg
*.asc
!docs/*.asc
!release/*.asc
secring.*
pubring.*
trustdb.gpg

# LUKS headers + recovery keys (CRITICAL — never commit)
luks-header-*.bin
luks-header-*.img
*-recovery.key
*-recovery.txt
luks-backup-*

# AWS/cloud credentials
.aws/
.gcp/
.azure/
credentials
credentials.json

# Passwords + tokens
*password*
*passwd*
!etc/pam.d/system-auth
!etc/security/faillock.conf
*.token
.netrc

# ============================================================
# Host-specific data (private info — sanitize before commit)
# ============================================================

# Host audit dumps (raw captures — contain MACs, UUIDs, VPN keys,
# hostnames, installed-package histories, kernel versions of a specific
# reference host). Kept locally for author's build reference, NOT shipped.
discovery/reference/
discovery/*.txt
discovery/kspp-live-audit.json

# Note: the discovery/ directory was retired 2026-05-12. Per-module design
# rationale is retained in each snippet's header/body and its history in Git.
# The patterns above remain as a defensive guard in case host-audit dumps land
# under discovery/ again.

# Backups of live /etc configs
etc-backup-*/
configs-snapshot-*/
backups/

# Developer continuation notes (session context for Claude Code).
# Contains author-specific context + chat history. NOT part of public repo.
CONTINUE.md
.claude/
.claude-*


# ============================================================
# Editor + OS artifacts
# ============================================================

# Editor swap + backup files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*

# macOS/Linux filesystem noise
.DS_Store
.Trash-*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Shell history / caches
.bash_history
.zsh_history
.sh_history

# ============================================================
# Test / CI artifacts
# ============================================================

tests/*.log
tests/output/
.shellcheck.cache

# ============================================================
# Audit FP false-trails (things that should be in repo):
# explicit negative patterns where above globs are too greedy
# ============================================================

# Keep these committed even though their patterns could match
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!docs/*.md
!docs/fp-database.md
!kickstart/snippets/*.ks
!post-install/*
!tests/*.sh
!tests/README.md

# branding/SHA256SUMS is the manifest
# of all branding asset hashes. Module 32 fetches it at build time
# and SHA-verifies each branding payload before installing into the
# image. The generic `SHA256SUMS` rule above (intended for build-output/
# and build-archive/ ISO checksums) would otherwise hide this.
!branding/SHA256SUMS

# Build artifacts (regenerable from firefox/*.js via scripts/regen-firefox-embed.sh)
firefox/.noid-firefox-hardening.js.gz.b64

# Build/install logs that accumulate inside kickstart/snippets/ during build
# (audit 2026-05-01). Source of truth lives in virt-install.log
# at repo root or under build-output/. Snippet-dir copies are stale by
# definition and should be cleaned between builds.
kickstart/snippets/livemedia.log
kickstart/snippets/virt-install.log
kickstart/snippets/program.log
kickstart/snippets/*.log

# Test scratch trees. Several structural tests place their working directory
# inside the checkout on purpose, so the extracted payloads share the
# repository filesystem. Untracked is not enough: a `git add -A` during a
# concurrent run committed 28 such files once, so the pattern is ignored and
# tests/00-compose-sources.sh additionally refuses to let one become tracked.
.test-*/
